# cinder_viz.conf — OPTIONAL visualiser config for cinder-home.
#
# Copy this to /contents/cinder_viz.conf on the device to turn ON the REAL audio-reactive
# visualiser, which is driven by Sony's built-in spectrum analyzer (AudioAnalyzerService). With
# this file ABSENT (the default), the visualiser still animates — synthetically — so there is zero
# boot risk in shipping nothing.
#
# DO NOT enable this until you have validated the analyzer on the device, because it dlopens and
# connects to a Sony audio service (a fresh runtime risk surface). Validate first:
#
#     adb push cinder-home/dist/cinder-probe /data/local/tmp/
#     # start music playing on the device, then:
#     adb shell 'cd /data/local/tmp && \
#       LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/system/vendor/sony/lib:/system/vendor/unknown321/lib:/system/lib:/usr/lib:/lib \
#       ./cinder-probe --analyzer'
#
# A PASS prints "frames flowed" plus the raw band values. If you see "started but NO frames", try
# `./cinder-probe --analyzer 0` (LEVEL mode) and confirm audio is actually playing. Note the raw
# band range it prints — if it is not roughly 0..(a few hundred) linear or 0..-60 dB, tune
# spectrum::from_bands in cinder-ffi before enabling. Only once the probe passes, set:

analyzer=1

# Everything in cinder-home that touches the analyzer runs behind the crash+hang guard, and the
# stream is stopped automatically when the player goes to the background. To turn it back off,
# delete this file (or change the line to anything other than `analyzer=1`).
